[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"PHP Reflection: A Deep Dive"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"Reflection in PHP is a powerful API that allows you to inspect and manipulate classes, interfaces, functions, methods, and extensions at runtime. It provides a way to analyze code structure and behavior without executing it directly. This is particularly useful for tasks like dependency injection, automated testing, documentation generation, and building dynamic frameworks."},{"order":3,"type":"subheading","text":"Core Reflection Classes"},{"order":4,"type":"paragraph","text":"The Reflection API is built around several core classes, each representing a different aspect of the code being reflected upon. Here are some of the most important ones:"},{"order":5,"type":"bullet_point","text":"ReflectionClass: Represents a class or interface."},{"order":6,"type":"bullet_point","text":"ReflectionMethod: Represents a method of a class."},{"order":7,"type":"bullet_point","text":"ReflectionFunction: Represents a function."},{"order":8,"type":"bullet_point","text":"ReflectionParameter: Represents a parameter of a function or method."},{"order":9,"type":"bullet_point","text":"ReflectionProperty: Represents a property of a class."},{"order":10,"type":"bullet_point","text":"ReflectionExtension: Represents a PHP extension."},{"order":11,"type":"subheading","text":"Basic Usage: Reflecting a Class"},{"order":12,"type":"paragraph","text":"Let's start with a simple example of reflecting a class. Suppose we have the following class:"},{"order":13,"type":"code","text":"<?php
class MyClass {
 public $publicProperty = 'public';
 private $privateProperty = 'private';

 public function publicMethod($param1, $param2) {
  // ...
 }

 private function privateMethod() {
  // ...
 }
}
?>"},{"order":14,"type":"paragraph","text":"To reflect this class, we can use the `ReflectionClass` class:"},{"order":15,"type":"code","text":"<?php
$reflection = new ReflectionClass('MyClass');

echo 'Class Name: ' . $reflection->getName() . "\n";
echo 'Is internal: ' . ($reflection->isInternal() ? 'Yes' : 'No') . "\n";
echo 'Is user defined: ' . ($reflection->isUserDefined() ? 'Yes' : 'No') . "\n";
?>"},{"order":16,"type":"subheading","text":"Accessing Methods and Properties"},{"order":17,"type":"paragraph","text":"You can retrieve information about the methods and properties of a class using the `getMethods()` and `getProperties()` methods of the `ReflectionClass` object."},{"order":18,"type":"code","text":"<?php
$reflection = new ReflectionClass('MyClass');

echo "Methods:\n";
foreach ($reflection->getMethods() as $method) {
 echo ' - ' . $method->getName() . "\n";
}

echo "Properties:\n";
foreach ($reflection->getProperties() as $property) {
 echo ' - ' . $property->getName() . "\n";
}
?>"},{"order":19,"type":"paragraph","text":"You can also filter methods and properties based on their visibility (public, private, protected) using flags. For example:"},{"order":20,"type":"code","text":"<?php
$reflection = new ReflectionClass('MyClass');

echo "Public Properties:\n";
foreach ($reflection->getProperties(ReflectionProperty::IS_PUBLIC) as $property) {
 echo ' - ' . $property->getName() . "\n";
}
?>"},{"order":21,"type":"subheading","text":"Working with Method Parameters"},{"order":22,"type":"paragraph","text":"The `ReflectionMethod` class allows you to inspect the parameters of a method. You can get the parameters using the `getParameters()` method."},{"order":23,"type":"code","text":"<?php
$reflection = new ReflectionClass('MyClass');
$method = $reflection->getMethod('publicMethod');

echo "Parameters for publicMethod:\n";
foreach ($method->getParameters() as $parameter) {
 echo ' - ' . $parameter->getName() . "\n";
}
?>"},{"order":24,"type":"subheading","text":"Dynamically Calling Methods"},{"order":25,"type":"paragraph","text":"Reflection can also be used to dynamically call methods, even private ones. This requires setting the method's accessibility to true using `setAccessible(true)`."},{"order":26,"type":"code","text":"<?php
$reflection = new ReflectionClass('MyClass');
$method = $reflection->getMethod('privateMethod');
$method->setAccessible(true); // Allow access to private method

$instance = new MyClass();
$method->invoke($instance); // Call the method
?>"},{"order":27,"type":"subheading","text":"Practical Applications"},{"order":28,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Dependency Injection: Reflection can be used to automatically inject dependencies into classes based on their constructor parameters."},{"order":29,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Automated Testing: Reflection can help in creating dynamic test cases by inspecting class structure and methods."},{"order":30,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Documentation Generation: Tools like phpDocumentor use reflection to extract information about classes, methods, and parameters to generate API documentation."},{"order":31,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Framework Development: Frameworks often use reflection to handle routing, configuration, and other dynamic aspects of the application."},{"order":32,"type":"subheading","text":"Conclusion"},{"order":33,"type":"paragraph","text":"PHP Reflection is a powerful tool for analyzing and manipulating code at runtime. While it can add complexity to your code, it provides flexibility and enables advanced programming techniques. Understanding the core concepts and classes of the Reflection API is essential for building robust and dynamic PHP applications."}]
